  "note": "Triennial election of Belfast Corporation, polled Wednesday 21 May 1958: 90 candidates for 53 seats (45 councillors and the aldermen of eight wards); contests in 13 of the 15 wards (Belfast News-Letter, 8 and 9 May 1958). Victoria Ward's councillors were elected on 19 June 1958 (separate folder) after the death of a candidate. Two Dock Irish Labour gains from the Unionists, after a recount. The printed majority (52 in the News-Letter, 24 in the Irish News) does not match the printed votes and is not recorded. The Irish News labels the Fitt and O'Kane ticket Dock Irish Labour."
